#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:68
msgid "A **driver** is a package that knows the network protocol of one kind of database: `oracledb` for Oracle, `pyodbc` for MS SQL Server, `psycopg` for PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:70
msgid "All drivers follow the same standard, the **DB-API** (PEP 249): `connect`, `cursor`, `execute`, `fetchall`, `commit`, `close`. What you learn today with SQLite works with your database too - only the `connect` line changes (section 7)."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:73
msgid "**SQLite** is a database in a single file. The module `sqlite3` comes with Python - nothing to install, no server. Perfect for learning, for tests and for small local data marts."
msgstr ""

