#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:431
msgid "Why never an f-string: SQL injection"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:433
msgid "It is tempting to build the SQL text with an f-string. Do not - with values from outside (a file, a form, a parameter of a script), the text can **change the query**:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:449
msgid "With a parameter, the driver sends the value **as a value** - it can never become SQL. Parameters also handle quotes in names (`O'Neil`), dates and numbers correctly, and let the database reuse the query plan."
msgstr ""

