msgid "Never a password in the code"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:1121
msgid "A password in a script, a notebook or a config file ends up in Git, in e-mails and in backups (session 10). Ways to keep it out:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:1124
msgid "**Windows login** (trusted connection, Kerberos) - no password at all, if your database supports it; the best option."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:1126
msgid "**environment variables** (session 10) - set per user, read with `os.environ`."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:1127
msgid "the **keyring** package - stores the password in the Windows Credential Manager."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/13-databases.md:1128
msgid "a `.env` file **listed in `.gitignore`**, read with the `python-dotenv` package."
msgstr ""

